I quit my job to be self employed and so lost my health plan that my employer provided me With that plan we could go to the doctor and pay 30$ co-pay. All I could buy in the health insurance market was Obama care. There were no options to choose from only gold or silver plans from providence. Now to go to the doctor we have to satisfy a 6500$ deductible per person before the insurance co. pays a dime. My Obama-care plan cost 1637$ per month and my old plan my employer paid for was just shy of 1400$ per month. Great deal???
I am looking forward to something better from Mr. Trump. Even if we went back to what I had it would let us go to the doctor which now we can not do due to the fact we can not afford the deductible.

@tempsperdue
Not disingenuous but I object to PR and will most certainly draw attention to implementations of PR I consider failures.  Enough folks post here who think going to PR will create world peace and cure the common cold and they seem to do this without considering the failures.  Germany and the Scandinavian countries are good examples where PR works as well as it can work.  But since many people want PR since that would  "make every vote count" how do you propose to implement a htreshold which does throw away votes?  

As an aside (I know its not your point) making every vote count is a chimera anyway.  Run an election with PR.  Have 6 parties all with some number of seats.  They now go away and scheme and negotiate with each other until a coalition government forms with at least 50% plus 1 vote.  So, do the votes of the other 49% count anymore?  NO, they are not in the coalition.  Votes for the losers are always wasted.  Welcome to voting and democracy folks.

