A lot of posts are asking what the cost of this project will be. That all depends on a great number of variables which are not yet known. For example:

1) How many of the 18 airframes will be single-seaters and two-seaters;
2) How much in the way of spare parts, tools and test equipment, logistical support will be required to put them into service;
3) How many spare enginse, radar sets, secure radios, etc., will be needed;
4) Will DND buy cockpit simulators to train the pilots;
5) How long you intend to keep 'em flying? Government procurement rules oblige DND to specify the lifespan of the item so that operations and maintenance costs can be estimated. Will the Super Hornets be retired once the 'new' fighter is acquired? If so, when will that be? (NB: the US Navy has stated that this plane will cease to be combat viable after 2035.)

Also, what are the added costs of training an operating now that the air force will have a mixed fleet? The CF18 and Super Hornet are different animals.

